+# LiveKit AgentSession cascaded provider (`livekit_session`)
+
+A τ-bench audio-native provider whose agent is a real `livekit.agents.AgentSession`
+running the cascaded pipeline (Deepgram nova-3 → gpt-4.1 → Deepgram Aura by default).
+
+| | `livekit` (built-in) | `livekit_session` (this module) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Pipeline | LiveKit *plugins* called directly | `AgentSession` + `Agent` |
+| Turn end | Deepgram VAD endpointing (`endpointing_ms`) | LiveKit turn detector / VAD / STT endpointing (`TurnHandlingOptions`) |
+| Barge-in | instant on any STT speech event | LiveKit interruption handling (adaptive model or VAD, min duration/words, false-interruption resume) |
+| Preemptive generation | no | yes (LiveKit default) |
+| Tool execution | provider parses LLM tool calls | LiveKit function tools bridged to τ-bench (results next tick) |
+| Extra outputs | – | `livekit_events.jsonl` sidecar per simulation |
+
+```
+tau2 run --domain retail --audio-native --audio-native-provider livekit_session \
+    --cascaded-config cascaded-session --speech-complexity regular --verbose-logs
+```
+
+Presets (`config.py::SESSION_CONFIGS`): `cascaded-session` (turn detector + adaptive
+interruptions; needs LiveKit Cloud credentials for the hosted v1 detector and the
+adaptive model), `cascaded-session-mini` (local v1-mini detector), `cascaded-session-vad`
+(VAD-only turn taking and interruptions; config ablation).
+
+`--agent-prompt-file <file>` replaces the instruction block of the system prompt
+(the domain policy is still appended). Any prompt/turn-handling change makes a
+leaderboard submission "custom".
+
+## How a tick works
+
+1. Pending τ-bench tool results resolve the futures of the bridged LiveKit tools.
+2. The tick's user audio (G.711 8 kHz) is converted to 16 kHz PCM and pushed into
+   `TickAudioInput` as 20 ms frames.
+3. Events from the session (transcripts, state changes, tool calls, TTS text tokens,
+   usage) are drained from a queue until the tick deadline.
+4. Up to one tick of synthesized agent audio is pulled from `TickAudioOutput`
+   (LiveKit pushed it faster than real time), converted to G.711, and paired with a
+   proportional slice of the utterance transcript captured by `TickTextOutput`.
+5. `playback_finished` is reported to LiveKit only when the simulation has actually
+   drained a flushed segment, so the agent state machine follows simulated playback.
+   When LiveKit clears the output buffer (real interruption) the remaining audio is
+   discarded and reported as interrupted; a pause (possible false interruption) just
+   stops draining until resume.
+
+Sidecar records (`artifacts/task_<id>/sim_<uuid>/livekit_events.jsonl`):
+`user_input_transcribed`, `user_state_changed`, `agent_state_changed`,
+`overlapping_speech`, `agent_false_interruption`, `function_tools_executed`,
+`conversation_item_added`, `metrics_collected` (LLM/TTS/STT), `error`, `close`.
+
+## Tests
+
+```
+uv run pytest tests/test_voice/test_livekit_session_adapter.py -q            # pure tests
+TAU2_RUN_LIVEKIT_SESSION_TESTS=1 uv run pytest ... -k end_to_end -s        # needs Deepgram + OpenAI keys
+```
